# {{name}}: PostgreSQL with backups

Rendered by infralift from the `postgres-with-backups` stack into one AWS
account, region `{{region}}`. State: {{state_tool}}.

## What it creates

- `modules/database`: RDS PostgreSQL {{engine_version}} (`{{instance_class}}`,
  {{allocated_storage_gb}} GB gp3, encrypted) in the private subnets
  `{{subnet_ids}}` of `{{vpc_id}}`. Not publicly accessible. Its security
  group admits 5432 from one CIDR (the VPC's own range unless `allowed_cidr`
  says otherwise) and, when set, one security group. A parameter group
  requires TLS and logs statements slower than one second. Automated backups
  are kept {{backup_retention_days}} days for point-in-time restore. Deletion
  protection is on, and a deletion takes a final snapshot first.
- `modules/snapshot-exports`: an S3 bucket for snapshots exported out of RDS,
  encrypted with its own KMS key, with public access blocked, TLS required,
  versioning on, objects moved to Glacier Instant Retrieval after 30 days and
  deleted after {{export_retention_days}} days. Plus the IAM role RDS assumes
  to write an export there.

The master user is `dbadmin`. Its password is generated and rotated by RDS
in Secrets Manager; read it with
`aws secretsmanager get-secret-value --secret-id <db_master_user_secret_arn>`.
It is never in this code or in state.

## Exporting a snapshot

Nothing exports automatically. To copy a snapshot out of RDS, as Parquet:

```sh
aws rds start-export-task \
  --export-task-identifier {{name}}-$(date +%Y%m%d) \
  --source-arn <snapshot arn> \
  --s3-bucket-name <export_bucket> \
  --iam-role-arn <export_role_arn> \
  --kms-key-id <export_kms_key_arn>
```

## Cost

An estimate at list prices in us-east-1, checked 2026-11-14, not a quote. At
the defaults: db.t4g.micro single-AZ about $12/month, 20 GB of gp3 about
$2.30, the Secrets Manager secret $0.40 and the KMS key $1. About $16/month
before traffic. Automated backup storage up to the database's size is free;
exports cost per GB exported and stored. Larger instance classes cost much
more: db.m7g.large is roughly $120/month.

## Credentials

{{#if backend_r2}}| Variable | Where | What |
|---|---|---|
| `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` | repository secrets (read-only key), `production` environment secrets (write key) | The AWS account this project manages |
| `TFSTATE_R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `TFSTATE_R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` | repository secrets | An R2 API token's S3 credentials, object read and write on the state bucket |
| `TF_STATE_PASSPHRASE` | repository secret | Encrypts state and saved plans. Keep a copy: without it the state is unreadable |
| `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` | repository variable | The Cloudflare account that holds the state bucket |
{{/if}}{{#if backend_tfc}}| Variable | Where | What |
|---|---|---|
| `TF_API_TOKEN` | repository secret | A Terraform Cloud token that can plan and apply in workspace `{{tfc_workspace}}` |
| `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` | workspace environment variables (sensitive) | The AWS account this project manages |
{{/if}}
## First apply

{{#if backend_r2}}1. Create the state bucket once, from `bootstrap/`:
   `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=... tofu init && tofu apply -var cloudflare_account_id=...`
2. Set the credentials above, then merge this {{change_request}}. The push to
   main plans, and the `production` environment applies that saved plan.
{{/if}}{{#if backend_tfc}}1. Set the credentials above on the repository and the workspace, then merge
   this {{change_request}}. The push to main plans in Terraform Cloud, and the
   `production` environment confirms that run.
{{/if}}
A daily `infra drift` job plans main against what is running and fails if
anything changed outside Terraform.
